Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 5 — Xamarin / .NET Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn how to systematically understand Android applications built with Xamarin.Android, Xamarin.Forms, and .NET MAUI. Unlike Java/Kotlin applications, most application logic is written in C#, compiled into Common Intermediate Language (CIL/IL), and executed by the Mono/.NET runtime. By the end of this section, you should be able to reconstruct managed code architecture, runtime behavior, native integration, and the interaction between the .NET runtime and Android.



> Core Principle:
Xamarin applications are Android hosts for a managed .NET application. Reverse engineer the managed world first, then understand how it integrates with Android.




