Stage 29 — Common Xamarin Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Treating managed assemblies like Java classes.

Ignoring CIL metadata.

Confusing compiler-generated async state machines with handwritten logic.

Overlooking bindings between managed code and Android.

Assuming Xamarin.Forms or MAUI pages map directly to Android Activities.

Ignoring the .NET event model and property binding system.



---

Stage 30 — Xamarin / .NET APK Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify Xamarin.Android, Xamarin.Forms, and .NET MAUI applications.

✅ Reconstruct managed assemblies, namespaces, classes, and dependency graphs.

✅ Recover async workflows, iterator state machines, events, delegates, and property bindings.

✅ Understand managed-to-native interaction through Android bindings and JNI.

✅ Reconstruct navigation, MVVM architecture, persistence, networking, and state management.

✅ Distinguish framework infrastructure from handwritten application logic.

✅ Correlate runtime behavior with static reconstruction.

✅ Produce complete architectural documentation explaining both the managed .NET application and its Android integration.



